  "B11_notes": "Code default relation_boost is 0.20 (paper text says 0.35 and a -0.35*0.35 violation penalty, which is the superseded v1 scorer). All 14 relation-applied top-1 objects have pre-relation lexical score 1.0 (clipped), so the boost adds 0 and relation effect comes only from the sort-key tie-break; beta is inert in [0.2,0.5]. Graph top-1 scores take values <=0.375 or >=0.75, so thresholds 0.45 and 0.55 trigger identically; 0.35 changes low-confidence status for 3 queries (score 0.375) which still fall back for relation_unresolved.",
  "B4": "Yes (in-sample): benchmark built 2026-07-12 (4cc58e8); v1 scorer evaluated on the same 48 queries 2026-07-13 (ae9f120), relation reranking did not help; v3 scorer rewritten and reported on the same 48 queries 2026-07-24 (57e8b23); extended set reuses the 48 and adds no relational queries; no held-out ScanNet split.",
  "negative_accuracy_rule": "evaluate_grounding: negative_correct = (result.found is False) for verified-absence queries; run_grounding_variants sets found = (search.status == \"ok\"), status ok iff top candidate score > 0. So a lexical variant abstains only when no object has any label/text/synonym/affordance token overlap with the target. No calibrated threshold (0.45 only triggers fallback). flat_embedding never abstains (score=(cos+1)/2>0) -> 0.0."
}